<p>Israel said it carried out airstrikes in Gaza City on May 15 targeting Izz al-Din al-Haddad, whom Israeli officials described as the head of Hamas’ armed wing in Gaza and one of the planners of the Oct. 7, 2023, attack on Israel. Gaza medics said at least seven Palestinians were killed, including three women and a child, and at least 50 people were injured when strikes hit an apartment and a vehicle. Netanyahu and Defence Minister Israel Katz said they ordered the operation, and Haddad’s fate was not immediately clear. The strike occurred while Israel and Hamas remained stalled in talks over President Trump’s post-war plan for Gaza, after a U.S.-backed October ceasefire agreement intended to halt fighting.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/eYCNfK5aSpM29O7bZBgcYByKk17y_joP6CWz0VVAV9CUHClLADHmTqpy29kRIw4Yx3saPJVM5xwDWXYYrRAfIQV5qZbvy67kvGzkWTYB2Q' alt='A fire burns in a residential apartment after Israeli shelling, according to the Ministry of Health, in Gaza.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Strike site: Reports identified the main Gaza City strike location as the Rimal neighbourhood; Minute Mirror said the residential block was known locally as the Al-Mu’taz building.</li><li>Hamas succession: Haddad became Hamas’ military chief in the Gaza Strip after Israel killed commander Mohammad Sinwar in May 2025.</li><li>Negotiations angle: Ynet reported Haddad opposed disarmament and said Hamas was preparing to choose a new leader on Sunday.</li><li>Israeli warning: Protothema reported Netanyahu and Katz told Hamas figures, “Sooner or later Israel will find you”.</li></ul><blockquote>Today we control 60 per cent; tomorrow we shall see. - Benjamin Netanyahu</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Israeli government: The office of Defence Minister Israel Katz said Haddad was responsible for the “murder, abduction, and harm” of Israeli civilians and IDF soldiers. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/israel-targets-top-hamas-militant-leader-in-gaza-strike/article70984711.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Israeli security sources: Ynet said officials cited “initial indications” that the strike had succeeded, while Haaretz reported a senior security official saying the assassination attempt was successful. (<a href='https://www.ynetnews.com/article/s1nidcvjfe'>Ynetnews</a>, <a href='https://www.haaretz.com/gaza/2026-05-15/ty-article/.premium/israeli-strike-in-gaza-targets-hamas-military-head-in-the-strip-netanyahu-says/0000019e-2ca7-d605-abbe-edb7fa880000'>Haaretz</a>)</li><li>Hamas: Hamas did not immediately comment on Haddad’s fate and did not confirm Israel’s claim. (<a href='https://www.middleeastmonitor.com/20260515-israel-claims-it-targeted-hamas-military-chief-in-gaza-city-strike/'>Middle East Monitor</a>)</li><li>Gaza medics: Medics said emergency teams dealt with casualties at both the apartment building and vehicle strike sites. (<a href='https://english.aaj.tv/news/330459052/israel-targets-hamas-military-chief-in-gaza-strike'>Aaj English TV</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/israel-targets-head-of-hamas-armed-wing-with-gaza-strike'>Seven killed in Gaza as Israel says it targets Hamas leader</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/2000622/on-nakba-israel-claims-control-over-most-of-gaza-strip'>On Nakba, Israel claims control over most of Gaza Strip</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/israel-targets-top-hamas-militant-leader-in-gaza-strike/article70984711.ece'>Gaza airstrike targeted Hamas military wing leader, Israel says</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/israel-carries-out-strikes-in-gaza-targets-hamas-chief-11502432#publisher=newsstand'>Israel Carries Out Strikes In Gaza, Targets Hamas Chief</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/05/15/israeli-army-announces-targeting-of-hamas-military-chief-in-gaza-city-airstrike'>Israeli ar